# Vercel CLI (local, non-Git deploys) only honors .vercelignore -- it does
# NOT read .gitignore. Vercel's own CLI already hardcodes .env.local and
# .env.*.local into its default ignore list, but this repeats that exclusion
# explicitly (defense in depth) and adds the private/internal material
# .gitignore was never responsible for keeping out of a deployment.

# Env files -- redundant with Vercel's built-in default ignore list for
# .env.local specifically, kept explicit on purpose. .env.example is a
# template with no real values and is fine to include.
.env*
!.env.example

# Personal design references and the company brief -- not part of the
# running application, not meant for a shared deployment.
references/

# Internal audit trail and review artifacts -- not the company-facing
# report, and not needed to run the app.
docs/design-decisions.md
docs/final-inventory.md
docs/requirements-audit.md
docs/model-switcher-codex-review.md
docs/project-technical-guide.md
docs/remaining-work-plan.md
docs/submission-checklist.md

# Screenshots captured by browser test runs -- generated artifacts, not
# source, and not needed to run the app.
tests/browser/*.png

# AI-agent tooling instructions -- not part of the running application.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
